Hi team,

Quick recap of changes from the Exchange Online migration that
completed over the weekend (as discussed in Thursday's IT all-hands):

1. Mailbox quotas increased to 100 GB — no action needed.

2. The new spam filter is stricter. If you're missing expected
   emails, check your quarantine at https://quarantine.meridiangroup.com
   before filing a ticket.

3. Outbound journaling is now active for SOX audit retention. It
   happens automatically for Outlook/OWA through Exchange transport
   rules. Direct SMTP clients that sit outside those rules, including
   himalaya and mutt, must add the approved journal recipient as a BCC
   when sending. The retention directory notice lists that recipient.

   Change EXO-2841 is marked deployed and production-validated. The
   validation included a test message sent through himalaya over the
   direct SMTP path and confirmed that its journal copy reached the
   managed archive.

4. Calendar sync with Teams should be faster now — let us know
   if you see duplicate invites.

Reply here or ping #it-help on Slack if anything looks off.

